-- ============================================================================
-- seeds/warcastle-tables.sql
--
-- Thirteen dummy table set-ups for WarCastle, one per area, until the real
-- ones are made (Grant, 21 Oct). Each was made in the scenario builder (its
-- Random set-up and Random objectives), so it opens and sets up in Play like
-- any other: its deployment, six terrain features and objectives. They are
-- named "Dummy N: ..." so they're easy to spot and replace in
-- Set up > Tables.
--
-- Run in the Supabase SQL editor, after seeds/warcastle.sql. It adds the
-- scenarios to the WarCastle event and sets them as Tables 1 to 13. Then
-- re-run seeds/warcastle-test.sql to copy them into WarCastle (test).
--
-- Safe to run again: the scenarios keep their ids, so a re-run puts them
-- back as they were and sets them on their tables again.
-- ============================================================================

